{"status":"ready","content":"Let's solve this step by step:\r\n\r\n1) First, calculate the mean $\\bar{x}$:\r\n   • $\\bar{x} = \\frac{1 + 12 - 17 - 3 - 11 - 5}{6} = -\\frac{23}{6}$\r\n\r\n2) Subtract the mean from each value and square the differences:\r\n   • $(1 - (-\\frac{23}{6}))^2 = (1 + \\frac{23}{6})^2 = (\\frac{29}{6})^2 = \\frac{841}{36}$\r\n   • $(12 - (-\\frac{23}{6}))^2 = (12 + \\frac{23}{6})^2 = (\\frac{95}{6})^2 = \\frac{9025}{36}$\r\n   • $(-17 - (-\\frac{23}{6}))^2 = (-17 + \\frac{23}{6})^2 = (-\\frac{79}{6})^2 = \\frac{6241}{36}$\r\n   • $(-3 - (-\\frac{23}{6}))^2 = (-3 + \\frac{23}{6})^2 = (\\frac{5}{6})^2 = \\frac{25}{36}$\r\n   • $(-11 - (-\\frac{23}{6}))^2 = (-11 + \\frac{23}{6})^2 = (-\\frac{43}{6})^2 = \\frac{1849}{36}$\r\n   • $(-5 - (-\\frac{23}{6}))^2 = (-5 + \\frac{23}{6})^2 = (\\frac{8}{6})^2 = \\frac{64}{36}$\r\n\r\n3) Sum these squared differences:\r\n   • $\\frac{841 + 9025 + 6241 + 25 + 1849 + 64}{36} = \\frac{18045}{36} = 501.25$\r\n\r\n4) Divide by $(n-1) = 5$ and take the square root:\r\n   • $\\sqrt{\\frac{18045}{180}} = \\sqrt{\\frac{18045}{180}} = \\sqrt{100.25} = \\sqrt{\\frac{401}{4}} = \\frac{\\sqrt{401}}{2}$\r\n\r\n5) Therefore, the answer is $\\boxed{\\frac{\\sqrt{401}}{2}}$\r\n","path":"responses/claude-3-5-haiku/livebench-036-math.txt","size":1148,"mtime":1779363898}